module

public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.ArtinRees.AssociatedGradedRing
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.FiniteType.SyzygyCoefficients
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Conormal algebras of a presentation after a finite type extension of the coefficients

Let `B = C[x_1, …, x_n]/(f_1, …, f_m)` be a presentation of a `C`-algebra, let `D` be a
Noetherian `C`-algebra and let `I ⊆ D` be an ideal. For a ring map `σ : C → D` the fibre
`B ⊗_{C, σ} D` is the cokernel of the matrix of the `σ(f_j)` over `D[x_1, …, x_n]`, and the
conormal algebra of the closed subscheme of `Spec(B ⊗_{C, σ} D)` cut out by `I` is the
`I`-adic associated graded algebra `Gr_I(B ⊗_{C, σ} D)`. The main result produces a `C`-algebra
`C'` of finite type through which the structure map `C → D` factors, together with a bound `c`,
such that any ring map `τ' : C' → D` congruent to the given one modulo `I^{c+1}` induces a map
`σ' : C → D` with `Gr_I(B ⊗_{C, σ'} D) ≅ Gr_I(B ⊗_{C, σ} D)` as graded algebras.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.ConormalApproximation.relationMapOfHom`: the map `D[x]^{⊕m} → D[x]`,
  `v ↦ ∑_j v_j σ(f_j)`, attached to a ring map `σ : C → D` and a family of relations over `C`.
* `Stacks.ConormalApproximation.quotRangeEquivTensor`: its cokernel is `B ⊗_C D`.
* `Stacks.ConormalApproximation.map_symm_quotRangeEquivTensor_map_algebraMap`: under that
  identification the ideal `I` generates in the fibre is the image of the ideal `I` generates in
  `D[x_1, …, x_n]`, which is the ideal the associated graded comparison is taken for.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ConormalApproximation.congruentModPow_relationMapOfHom` and
  `Stacks.ConormalApproximation.congruentModPow_syzygyMap`: two ring maps agreeing modulo `I^k`
  give matrices congruent modulo the `k`-th power of the ideal generated by `I` in `D[x]`.
* `Stacks.ConormalApproximation.exists_finiteType_coefficients_associatedGraded_equiv`: the
  affine ring-level core of the proof of Stacks 0CAY, whose scheme-level statement is
  `exists_finiteType_pointed_extension_conormalAlgebra_iso`. Its comparison is disclosed to be
  induced by the identity of `D[x_1, …, x_n]`, which is what the gluing over the charts of `Y`
  needs.

## Implementation notes

The two matrices of the four-term complex come from Stacks 0CB0: the finite type algebra `C'`
carries polynomials `t_{kj}` whose images under the given map `τ : C' → D` are a generating set of
syzygies among the `σ(f_j)`, and the syzygy equations hold already over `C'`. Hence for any
`τ' : C' → D` the specialized matrices again form a complex, and congruence of `τ` with `τ'`
modulo `I^{c+1}` makes both matrices congruent modulo the `(c+1)`-st power of the ideal generated
by `I`. Exactness of the unprimed complex is Stacks 0CAZ, and the Artin-Rees bound `c` for both
unprimed matrices exists because `D[x_1, …, x_n]` is Noetherian. The comparison of associated
graded algebras is then the core of Stacks 07VF.

The conclusion is an `AssociatedGraded.GradedAlgEquiv`, the last step of the source's proof: the
comparison is induced by the identity of `D[x_1, …, x_n]`, so besides being an isomorphism of
graded modules over `Gr_I(D[x_1, …, x_n])` — recovered by
`AssociatedGraded.GradedAlgEquiv.toGradedLinearEquiv` — it respects the multiplication of the
two conormal algebras and their unit, by
`associatedGraded_coker_algEquiv_of_isArtinReesConstant`. Being induced by the identity is
*asserted* in the conclusion, not merely true of the construction: a bare
`AssociatedGraded.GradedAlgEquiv` does not determine the comparison on representatives, and
without that the comparisons over two charts of `Y` cannot be shown to agree after restriction.
That the graded pieces appearing here,
formed over the ambient ring `D[x_1, …, x_n]`, are those of the conormal algebra of the quotient
*ring* `B ⊗_{C, σ} D` for the ideal `I` generates there, is
`AssociatedGraded.pieceRestrictScalarsEquiv`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CAY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CAY)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CAZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CAZ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CB0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CB0)
* [Stacks Project, Section 15.4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07VD)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07VF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07VF)
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v w

namespace Stacks.ConormalApproximation

/-- The map `D[x_1, …, x_n]^{⊕m} → D[x_1, …, x_n]`, `v ↦ ∑_j v_j σ(f_j)`, attached to a ring map
`σ : C → D` and relations `f_1, …, f_m ∈ C[x_1, …, x_n]`. -/
noncomputable def relationMapOfHom {C : Type u} {D : Type w} [CommRing C] [CommRing D] {n m : ℕ}
    (σ : C →+* D) (r : Fin m → MvPolynomial (Fin n) C) :
    (Fin m → MvPolynomial (Fin n) D) →ₗ[MvPolynomial (Fin n) D] MvPolynomial (Fin n) D :=
  Fintype.linearCombination (MvPolynomial (Fin n) D) fun j => MvPolynomial.map σ (r j)

/-- `relationMapOfHom σ r` sends `v` to `∑_j v_j σ(r_j)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem relationMapOfHom_apply {C : Type u} {D : Type w} [CommRing C] [CommRing D] {n m : ℕ}
    (σ : C →+* D) (r : Fin m → MvPolynomial (Fin n) C) (v : Fin m → MvPolynomial (Fin n) D) :
    relationMapOfHom σ r v = ∑ j, v j * MvPolynomial.map σ (r j) := by
  simp [relationMapOfHom, Fintype.linearCombination_apply, smul_eq_mul]

/-- For the structure map `C → D`, `relationMapOfHom` applied to the relations of a presentation
`P` is `SyzygyCoefficients.relationMap D P`. -/
theorem relationMapOfHom_algebraMap {C : Type u} {B : Type v} {D : Type w}
    [CommRing C] [CommRing B] [CommRing D] [Algebra C B] [Algebra C D] {n m : ℕ}
    (P : Algebra.Presentation C B (Fin n) (Fin m)) :
    relationMapOfHom (algebraMap C D) P.relation = SyzygyCoefficients.relationMap D P := rfl

/-- The cokernel of `relationMapOfHom (algebraMap C D) P.relation` is `D ⊗_C B`, by Stacks 0CAZ. -/
noncomputable def quotRangeEquivTensor {C : Type u} {B : Type v} (D : Type w)
    [CommRing C] [CommRing B] [CommRing D] [Algebra C B] [Algebra C D] {n m : ℕ}
    (P : Algebra.Presentation C B (Fin n) (Fin m)) :
    (MvPolynomial (Fin n) D ⧸
        LinearMap.range (relationMapOfHom (algebraMap C D) P.relation)) ≃ₐ[D]
      TensorProduct C D B :=
  SyzygyCoefficients.quotRangeRelationMapEquiv D P

/-- **The identification of the cokernel with the base change, on a representative**: the class of
a polynomial `a ∈ D[x_1, …, x_n]` is carried to the value of `a` at the generators `1 ⊗ x_i` of
`B ⊗_{C,σ} D`. This is the only form in which the identification can be computed, and it is what
makes it natural in a presentation morphism. -/
theorem quotRangeEquivTensor_mk {C : Type u} {B : Type v} (D : Type w)
    [CommRing C] [CommRing B] [CommRing D] [Algebra C B] [Algebra C D] {n m : ℕ}
    (P : Algebra.Presentation C B (Fin n) (Fin m)) (a : MvPolynomial (Fin n) D) :
    quotRangeEquivTensor D P
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk (LinearMap.range (relationMapOfHom (algebraMap C D) P.relation)) a) =
      MvPolynomial.aeval (R := D) (fun i => (1 : D) ⊗ₜ[C] P.val i) a :=
  rfl

/-- **The identification of the cokernel with the base change is natural in a morphism of
presentations given by a renaming of the variables.** If `ι` names, among the generators of a
presentation `P'` of `B'`, the images under `res : B → B'` of the generators of a presentation `P`
of `B`, then renaming the variables along `ι` induces on the two cokernels the base change
`D ⊗_C res` of `res`.

This is the step that makes a family of chart presentations compatible with restriction, and the
*renaming* is what makes one ring map `D[x_1, …, x_n] → D[x_1, …, x_{n'}]` serve two different
`C`-algebra structures on `D` at once: `MvPolynomial.rename ι` does not mention the structure
map `C → D`, whereas lifting a generator through a presentation does. -/
theorem map_quotRangeEquivTensor_rename {C : Type u} {B B' : Type v} (D : Type w)
    [CommRing C] [CommRing B] [CommRing B'] [CommRing D] [Algebra C B] [Algebra C B']
    [Algebra C D] {n m n' m' : ℕ} (P : Algebra.Presentation C B (Fin n) (Fin m))
    (P' : Algebra.Presentation C B' (Fin n') (Fin m')) (res : B →ₐ[C] B')
    (ι : Fin n → Fin n') (hι : ∀ i, P'.val (ι i) = res (P.val i))
    (a : MvPolynomial (Fin n) D) :
    Algebra.TensorProduct.map (AlgHom.id C D) res
        (quotRangeEquivTensor D P
          (Ideal.Quotient.mk
            (LinearMap.range (relationMapOfHom (algebraMap C D) P.relation)) a)) =
      quotRangeEquivTensor D P'
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk (LinearMap.range (relationMapOfHom (algebraMap C D) P'.relation))
          (MvPolynomial.rename ι a)) := by
  rw [quotRangeEquivTensor_mk, quotRangeEquivTensor_mk]
  induction a using MvPolynomial.induction_on with
  | C d =>
      simp only [MvPolynomial.aeval_C, MvPolynomial.rename_C,
        Algebra.TensorProduct.algebraMap_apply, Algebra.TensorProduct.map_tmul, AlgHom.coe_id,
        id_eq, map_one]
  | add q₁ q₂ h₁ h₂ => simp only [map_add, h₁, h₂]
  | mul_X q i h =>
      simp only [map_mul, MvPolynomial.aeval_X, MvPolynomial.rename_X, h,
        Algebra.TensorProduct.map_tmul, map_one, hι i]

/-- **The ideal `I ⊆ D` cuts out the fibre in the chart.** Under the identification
`quotRangeEquivTensor` of the cokernel of the relation matrix with the base change
`B ⊗_{C,σ} D`, the ideal that `I` generates in that base change — the ideal of the closed
subscheme of `Spec(B ⊗_{C,σ} D)` cut out by `I`, which for `I` the maximal ideal of `D` is the
fibre `Y_t` — is the ideal that `I` generates in `D[x_1, …, x_n]` and then in the quotient. The
latter is the shape in which the `I`-adic filtration of the chart is taken over the ambient
polynomial ring, hence the shape
`exists_finiteType_coefficients_associatedGraded_equiv` compares. -/
theorem map_symm_quotRangeEquivTensor_map_algebraMap {C : Type u} {B : Type v} {D : Type w}
    [CommRing C] [CommRing B] [CommRing D] [Algebra C B] [Algebra C D] {n m : ℕ}
    (P : Algebra.Presentation C B (Fin n) (Fin m)) (I : Ideal D) :
    (I.map (algebraMap D (TensorProduct C D B))).map
        ((quotRangeEquivTensor D P).symm.toRingEquiv :
          TensorProduct C D B →+*
            MvPolynomial (Fin n) D ⧸
              LinearMap.range (relationMapOfHom (algebraMap C D) P.relation)) =
      (I.map (MvPolynomial.C : D →+* MvPolynomial (Fin n) D)).map
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk (LinearMap.range (relationMapOfHom (algebraMap C D) P.relation))) := by
  rw [Ideal.map_map, Ideal.map_map]
  congr 1
  exact RingHom.ext fun d => (quotRangeEquivTensor D P).symm.commutes d

/-- Two ring maps agreeing modulo an ideal `J` push a polynomial to two polynomials differing by
an element of the ideal generated by `J`. -/
theorem sub_map_mem_map_C {E : Type u} {D : Type w} [CommRing E] [CommRing D] {n : ℕ}
    (J : Ideal D) (σ σ' : E →+* D) (h : ∀ y, σ y - σ' y ∈ J) (p : MvPolynomial (Fin n) E) :
    MvPolynomial.map σ p - MvPolynomial.map σ' p ∈
      J.map (MvPolynomial.C : D →+* MvPolynomial (Fin n) D) := by
  induction p using MvPolynomial.induction_on with
  | C b =>
      have hc : MvPolynomial.map σ (MvPolynomial.C b) -
          MvPolynomial.map σ' (MvPolynomial.C b) =
          (MvPolynomial.C : D →+* MvPolynomial (Fin n) D) (σ b - σ' b) := by
        rw [MvPolynomial.map_C, MvPolynomial.map_C, ← map_sub]
      rw [hc]
      exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ (h b)
  | add p q hp hq => simpa [map_add, add_sub_add_comm] using Submodule.add_mem _ hp hq
  | mul_X p i hp =>
      have hx : MvPolynomial.map σ (p * MvPolynomial.X i) -
          MvPolynomial.map σ' (p * MvPolynomial.X i) =
          (MvPolynomial.map σ p - MvPolynomial.map σ' p) * MvPolynomial.X i := by
        simp [sub_mul]
      rw [hx]
      exact Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ hp

/-- Two ring maps agreeing modulo `I ^ k` push a polynomial to two polynomials differing by an
element of the `k`-th power of the ideal generated by `I`. -/
private theorem sub_map_mem_map_C_pow {E : Type u} {D : Type w} [CommRing E] [CommRing D] {n : ℕ}
    (I : Ideal D) (k : ℕ) (σ σ' : E →+* D) (h : ∀ y, σ y - σ' y ∈ I ^ k)
    (p : MvPolynomial (Fin n) E) :
    MvPolynomial.map σ p - MvPolynomial.map σ' p ∈
      (I.map (MvPolynomial.C : D →+* MvPolynomial (Fin n) D)) ^ k := by
  simpa [Ideal.map_pow] using sub_map_mem_map_C (I ^ k) σ σ' h p

private theorem mem_pow_smul_top_pi {A : Type*} [CommRing A] {m : ℕ} (K : Ideal A)
    {v : Fin m → A} (h : ∀ j, v j ∈ K) : v ∈ K • (⊤ : Submodule A (Fin m → A)) := by
  classical
  have hv : v = ∑ j, (Pi.single j (v j) : Fin m → A) := by
    funext i; simp [Finset.sum_apply, Pi.single_apply]
  rw [hv]
  refine Submodule.sum_mem _ fun j _ => ?_
  have hs : (Pi.single j (v j) : Fin m → A) = v j • (Pi.single j (1 : A) : Fin m → A) := by
    funext i; by_cases hij : i = j <;> simp [hij]
  rw [hs]
  exact Submodule.smul_mem_smul (h j) Submodule.mem_top

/-- If `σ` and `σ'` agree modulo `I^k`, the two relation matrices they define over
`D[x_1, …, x_n]` are congruent modulo the `k`-th power of the ideal generated by `I`. -/
theorem congruentModPow_relationMapOfHom {C : Type u} {D : Type w} [CommRing C] [CommRing D]
    {n m : ℕ} (I : Ideal D) (k : ℕ) (σ σ' : C →+* D) (r : Fin m → MvPolynomial (Fin n) C)
    (h : ∀ y : C, σ y - σ' y ∈ I ^ k) :
    CongruentModPow (I.map (MvPolynomial.C : D →+* MvPolynomial (Fin n) D))
      (relationMapOfHom σ r) (relationMapOfHom σ' r) k := by
  change LinearMap.range (relationMapOfHom σ r - relationMapOfHom σ' r) ≤ _
  rintro _ ⟨v, rfl⟩
  have hval : (relationMapOfHom σ r - relationMapOfHom σ' r) v =
      ∑ j, v j * (MvPolynomial.map σ (r j) - MvPolynomial.map σ' (r j)) := by
    simp [LinearMap.sub_apply, mul_sub, Finset.sum_sub_distrib]
  rw [hval]
  simpa using Ideal.sum_mem _ fun j (_ : j ∈ Finset.univ) =>
    Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (sub_map_mem_map_C_pow I k σ σ' h (r j))

/-- If `τ` and `τ'` agree modulo `I^k`, the two syzygy matrices obtained by specializing a matrix
of polynomials over `C'` are congruent modulo the `k`-th power of the ideal generated by `I`. -/
theorem congruentModPow_syzygyMap {C' : Type u} {D : Type w} [CommRing C'] [CommRing D]
    {n m K : ℕ} (I : Ideal D) (k : ℕ) (τ τ' : C' →+* D)
    (t : Fin K → Fin m → MvPolynomial (Fin n) C') (h : ∀ y : C', τ y - τ' y ∈ I ^ k) :
    CongruentModPow (I.map (MvPolynomial.C : D →+* MvPolynomial (Fin n) D))
      (SyzygyCoefficients.syzygyMap fun k j => MvPolynomial.map τ (t k j))
      (SyzygyCoefficients.syzygyMap fun k j => MvPolynomial.map τ' (t k j)) k := by
  change LinearMap.range (_ - _) ≤ _
  rintro _ ⟨w, rfl⟩
  refine mem_pow_smul_top_pi _ fun j => ?_
  have hval : ((SyzygyCoefficients.syzygyMap fun k j => MvPolynomial.map τ (t k j)) -
        (SyzygyCoefficients.syzygyMap fun k j => MvPolynomial.map τ' (t k j))) w j =
      ∑ kk, w kk * (MvPolynomial.map τ (t kk j) - MvPolynomial.map τ' (t kk j)) := by
    simp [LinearMap.sub_apply, mul_sub, Finset.sum_sub_distrib]
  rw [hval]
  exact Ideal.sum_mem _ fun kk (_ : kk ∈ Finset.univ) =>
    Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (sub_map_mem_map_C_pow I k τ τ' h (t kk j))

/-- **Stacks 0CAY**, affine case, with the congruence hypothesis `hcongr` over the finite type
extension explicit.
Let `B = C[x_1, …, x_n]/(f_1, …, f_m)` over `C`, let `D` be a Noetherian `C`-algebra and
`I ⊆ D` an ideal. There are a `C`-algebra `C'` of finite type, a `C`-algebra map `τ : C' → D`
and a bound `c` such that every ring map `τ' : C' → D` with `τ y - τ' y ∈ I^{c+1}` for all `y`
yields `σ' = τ' ∘ (C → C')` whose fibre `B ⊗_{C, σ'} D` has the same `I`-adic associated graded
algebra over `Gr_I(D[x_1, …, x_n])` as `B ⊗_C D`, that is, the same conormal algebra of the
closed subscheme cut out by `I`.

The comparison is *induced by the identity* of `D[x_1, …, x_n]`, by
`associatedGraded_coker_algEquiv_isInducedByIdentity`, and that is disclosed: it is what makes
the comparisons over two charts of `Y` compatible with restriction, hence what lets them be
glued (`Stacks.Conormal.commonChartAssociatedGradedEquivOfPresentations`).

This is the affine ring-level core of the proof of Tag 0CAY -- the graded comparison over a
presentation -- and not the tag itself. The full statement of that tag is
`exists_finiteType_pointed_extension_conormalAlgebra_iso_of_isLocalHom`. -/
theorem exists_finiteType_coefficients_associatedGraded_equiv
    {C : Type u} {B : Type v} {D : Type w}
    [CommRing C] [CommRing B] [CommRing D] [Algebra C B] [Algebra C D] [IsNoetherianRing D]
    {n m : ℕ} (P : Algebra.Presentation C B (Fin n) (Fin m)) (I : Ideal D) :
    ∃ (C' : Type u) (_ : CommRing C') (_ : Algebra C C') (_ : Algebra.FiniteType C C')
      (τ : C' →ₐ[C] D) (c : ℕ),
      ∀ τ' : C' →+* D,
        (∀ y : C', (τ : C' →+* D) y - τ' y ∈ I ^ (c + 1)) →
        ∃ eq : AssociatedGraded.GradedAlgEquiv
          (I.map (MvPolynomial.C : D →+* MvPolynomial (Fin n) D))
          (MvPolynomial (Fin n) D ⧸
            LinearMap.range (relationMapOfHom (algebraMap C D) P.relation))
          (MvPolynomial (Fin n) D ⧸
            LinearMap.range (relationMapOfHom (τ'.comp (algebraMap C C')) P.relation)),
          eq.IsInducedByIdentity := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨K, a, ha, hker⟩ := SyzygyCoefficients.exists_exact_resolution D P
  have hgen : ∀ v : Fin m → MvPolynomial (Fin n) D,
      (∑ j, v j * MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap C D) (P.relation j) = 0) →
      ∃ w : Fin K → MvPolynomial (Fin n) D, ∀ j, v j = ∑ k, w k * a k j := by
    intro v hv
    have hv' : v ∈ LinearMap.ker (SyzygyCoefficients.relationMap D P) := by
      simpa [LinearMap.mem_ker] using hv
    rw [hker] at hv'
    obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := hv'
    exact ⟨w, fun j => by rw [← hw, SyzygyCoefficients.syzygyMap_apply]⟩
  obtain ⟨C', _, _, _, τ, t, hsyz, hta, -, -, -⟩ :=
    SyzygyCoefficients.exists_finiteType_resolution P a ha hgen
  have hat : (fun k j => MvPolynomial.map (τ : C' →+* D) (t k j)) = a := by
    funext k j; exact hta k j
  obtain ⟨c₁, hc₁⟩ :=
    exists_isArtinReesConstant (I.map (MvPolynomial.C : D →+* MvPolynomial (Fin n) D))
      (SyzygyCoefficients.syzygyMap a)
  obtain ⟨c₂, hc₂⟩ :=
    exists_isArtinReesConstant (I.map (MvPolynomial.C : D →+* MvPolynomial (Fin n) D))
      (relationMapOfHom (algebraMap C D) P.relation)
  refine ⟨C', inferInstance, inferInstance, inferInstance, τ, max c₁ c₂, ?_⟩
  intro τ' hcongr
  have hbase : ∀ x : C, algebraMap C D x - (τ'.comp (algebraMap C C')) x ∈
      I ^ (max c₁ c₂ + 1) := by
    intro x
    have hx := hcongr (algebraMap C C' x)
    rwa [show (τ : C' →+* D) (algebraMap C C' x) = algebraMap C D x from τ.commutes x] at hx
  have hgg' : CongruentModPow (I.map (MvPolynomial.C : D →+* MvPolynomial (Fin n) D))
      (relationMapOfHom (algebraMap C D) P.relation)
      (relationMapOfHom (τ'.comp (algebraMap C C')) P.relation) (max c₁ c₂ + 1) :=
    congruentModPow_relationMapOfHom I (max c₁ c₂ + 1) _ _ P.relation hbase
  have hff' : CongruentModPow (I.map (MvPolynomial.C : D →+* MvPolynomial (Fin n) D))
      (SyzygyCoefficients.syzygyMap a)
      (SyzygyCoefficients.syzygyMap fun k j => MvPolynomial.map τ' (t k j))
      (max c₁ c₂ + 1) := by
    have hcong := congruentModPow_syzygyMap I (max c₁ c₂ + 1) (τ : C' →+* D) τ' t hcongr
    rwa [hat] at hcong
  have hcomplex : (relationMapOfHom (τ'.comp (algebraMap C C')) P.relation).comp
      (SyzygyCoefficients.syzygyMap fun k j => MvPolynomial.map τ' (t k j)) = 0 := by
    refine LinearMap.ext fun w => ?_
    have key : ∀ k, ∑ j, MvPolynomial.map τ' (t k j) *
        MvPolynomial.map (τ'.comp (algebraMap C C')) (P.relation j) = 0 := by
      intro k
      have h0 := congrArg (MvPolynomial.map τ') (hsyz k)
      simpa [map_sum, MvPolynomial.map_map] using h0
    simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearMap.zero_apply, relationMapOfHom_apply,
      SyzygyCoefficients.syzygyMap_apply, Finset.sum_mul]
    rw [Finset.sum_comm]
    refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun k _ => ?_
    have hassoc : ∀ j : Fin m, w k * MvPolynomial.map τ' (t k j) *
        MvPolynomial.map (τ'.comp (algebraMap C C')) (P.relation j) =
        w k * (MvPolynomial.map τ' (t k j) *
          MvPolynomial.map (τ'.comp (algebraMap C C')) (P.relation j)) :=
      fun j => mul_assoc _ _ _
    simp only [hassoc, ← Finset.mul_sum, key k, mul_zero]
  have hexact : LinearMap.ker (relationMapOfHom (algebraMap C D) P.relation) =
      LinearMap.range (SyzygyCoefficients.syzygyMap a) := hker
  have hg : IsArtinReesConstant (I.map (MvPolynomial.C : D →+* MvPolynomial (Fin n) D))
      (relationMapOfHom (algebraMap C D) P.relation) (max c₁ c₂) :=
    hc₂.mono (le_max_right _ _)
  have hg' := isArtinReesConstant_of_congr
    (I.map (MvPolynomial.C : D →+* MvPolynomial (Fin n) D))
    (SyzygyCoefficients.syzygyMap a)
    (SyzygyCoefficients.syzygyMap fun k j => MvPolynomial.map τ' (t k j))
    (relationMapOfHom (algebraMap C D) P.relation)
    (relationMapOfHom (τ'.comp (algebraMap C C')) P.relation)
    (max c₁ c₂) hcomplex (hc₁.mono (le_max_left _ _)) hg hexact hff' hgg'
  exact ⟨associatedGraded_coker_algEquiv_of_isArtinReesConstant
      (I.map (MvPolynomial.C : D →+* MvPolynomial (Fin n) D)) _ _ (max c₁ c₂) hg hg' hgg',
    associatedGraded_coker_algEquiv_isInducedByIdentity
      (I.map (MvPolynomial.C : D →+* MvPolynomial (Fin n) D)) _ _ (max c₁ c₂) hg hg' hgg'⟩

